    public void EverySourceOfAPairBinderAgreesInAnyOrder(string source, string records)
        => Assert.Equal(records, DiagnosticCorpus.RecordProfile(source));

    // SPEC 10.8 (the owner's O-263 (a)): two phases, whatever the order. The exact sources of a pair binder, an occurrence of the
    // original or an application of a bare slot, fix it first; an application whose target has its own layer (`s/(ref/i32)`) is no
    // evidence: it is formed under the fixed binder, so under owner it is the target itself (n1, n2; o1 and its swapped twin o1s; in
    // one argument o2, o2s; in one Tuple literal o3, o3s; from the expected result alone o4, and in either order of the result's parts
    // o6, o6s; a reference o7, o7s; a slot only the formed application binds o8, o8s, o9, o9s). An argument fits the formed Type by
    // SPEC 10.2's adaptation, as any argument fits its parameter (the owner's O-283 (a)): `rr: ref/(ref/i32)` takes a formed ref/i32
    // as one shared reference through layers, in either order, whatever fixes the binder: a bare slot (o1x2, o1x2s), a typed original
    // (q4, q4s) or a Literal's default (L2, L2s); an owned argument binds a formed ref/X's X (o9x, o9xs); 87d5653c2 compared the
    // argument's own Type and rejected them all. An exact source is never adapted to a formed layer, so a Place there is owner evidence
    // against ref in either order (e1, e1s). A Literal is no evidence (SPEC 10.5.1, 10.2.1; the owner's O-294 (b)): its default fits
    // every pair layer whose binder evidence fixed, an exact source or the original, as a borrowed temporary under ref, and binds only
    // what no evidence binds (e2, e2s; in a Tuple literal e2t, e2ts; at an original whose Type evidence bound e2w, e2ws; the other
    // 10.5.1 Literals, a control-flow one e2j and a literal-only expression e2e; in a Case payload cq1, cq1s; invalid where another
    // input binds the slot to a Type it does not fit, e2x, e2xs, cqx, cqxs, or where only an exclusive borrow of the temporary would fit,
    // e2u, e2us), while a suffixed literal is evidence (e2k, e2ks). A closed leaf target (`s/i64`) has no layer, structure or slot of
    // its own, so it is an exact source as a bare slot is: a typed argument there (a suffixed literal, a Place, a call result) is
    // owner evidence against ref in either order and over two overloads (Nc3t, N3a, c1s, c2, c2s, c3, c3s; at depth c9; a ref Place
    // against owner c7, c7s), agreeing evidence is accepted (c4, c4s, c5, c5s; at depth c9o), it alone fixes the binder (c8; from
    // the expected result c12; a constructor's own pattern c13, c13s, c13v) and a Literal there is no evidence (c6, c6s); G812's
    // 2f4bec489 formed it, accepted Nc3t, N3a, c1s-c3s, c7, c7s, c13, c13s and rejected c8. The owner's O-338 (a) settles that
    // reading (one rule for every pair layer): a ref argument at a closed leaf against owner evidence and an owner one against ref
    // are invalid in either order (X1, X1r; vr1, vr1s; at depth below a declared ref layer ol2, ol2s; in a Tuple literal T1;
    // from the argument against the expected result X2e); dev accepted T1, X2e and ol2s (its class 1). A closed target with
    // structure stays formed (c10). With only Literals at a pair, no evidence fixes the binder before selection, so a Literal at an
    // exact source checks no shape there; after selection the defaults bind it owner and the Literal fits the target the layer
    // fixes (the owner's O-343 (a)): at a closed leaf (P1) and at a solved slot another argument binds (P2), as dev; with evidence
    // fixing the binder the Literal fits the formed layer (P1r, P2r, P1t, P2t). G812's head rejected P2, and the fix also P1.
    // The rule is order-free (the owner's O-347 (a)): where the default has nothing to bind, a layer whose target is complete, it
    // is neither checked nor inferred, so the arguments' order, named arguments and an expected closed-leaf result give one verdict
    // (Qp1s, Rp1-Rp5, Qp2s, Rp7; Qe1, Qe2, Re4; f5a09feda rejected Qp1s, Rp2, Rp3, Rp5, Qp2s, Rp7, Qe1, Qe2, Re4). With G915, a
    // Literal-only slot against a borrowing plain candidate is ambiguous (Nc2, Nc2s, Nc3, Nc6), typed evidence decides (Nc1t, Nc2t,
    // Nc7). A formed Type no adaptation fits rejects in either order (L2y,
    // L2ys, q4y, q4ys, o3x, o3xs, o4x), and with
    // nothing to fix the binder it is unbound (o5); with no evidence a Literal's default fixes the binder after the defaults (L1, L1s),
    // and a formed layer's slot is bound then (d1, d1s; d1x invalid). a9497632c rejected o1, o2, o3, o4, o6, o7, o8 and o9 and accepted their swapped
    // twins; each order twin's invalid counterpart rejects in both orders (o2x, o2xs; r4f4x, r4f4xs for o6; o7x, o7xs; o8x, o8xs). A
    // slot fixed before any evidence is not being inferred (the owner's O-276 (a), as O-340 (a) reads it): `s/V` over an enclosing
    // slot its qualifier fixes to a Type with a layer, structure or slot of its own is formed, through a constructor (z1, z1s, z1x,
    // z1o), a method (z2, z2s) or a Case's payloads (z4, z4s, z4o, z4x, z4xs) alike; one fixed to a closed leaf reads as that leaf,
    // evidence on both paths (O-340 (a): c11, c11s through a constructor, c14, c14s through a method, invalid as on dev);
    // a326bfea7 read it as an exact source and rejected z1, z1s, z4 and z4s. A ref binder's formed ref/(ref/X) takes no ref/i32
    // reference slot, which is never borrowed implicitly (o9y, o9ys: o9's and o9s's invalid twins), while two layers fit (o9r, o9rs).
    // A call-shape contract (SPEC 7.4.4) holds where an argument needs the formed Type's adaptation, the relied-on slot a pair binder
    // (n1c, n1cs) or X beside a formed ref/X (n1d, n1ds), and their invalid twins reject in either order (n1cx, n1cxs, n1dx, n1dxs):
    // its collection precedes the sources that fix a binder and enters no application.
    // Under a binding that forms no Type (a pair target alone or an unresolved projection no premise proves owner, PLAN G886), a Type
    // formed under it, its standalone target or its pair layer's outer-Origin slot is not represented, so the call is one located
    // Unsupported_Kd (DECISIONS D3, temporary until G886's representation; F's ruling of 11-15): valid (f1n, f1ns, a Never argument)
    // and invalid alike (f1e; dt2, whose `W is Tag` needs the target; ow1p, ow1ps, whose premise is unproven). Box at the closed leaf
    // `s/Box` against U's undetermined evidence is IsSource's Language verdict first (C-359 B1, F's O1 (a)): f1, f1s, f1a. A plain
    // Type parameter has a selector of its own (f1x, f1xn, dt2x) and a premise proving owner forms (f1o). 9a0248f9f gave f1, f1s, f1e,
    // f1a, f1n, f1ns, ow1p and ow1ps NoApplicableOverload_Kd and accepted dt2. The same fact outside a call's trial: a function item's
    // signature at its value call (fr4n valid, fr4c invalid; 076e81d65 gave both NotCallable_Kd and 2f4bec489 accepted fr4c); a
    // constructor's Box at `s/Box` (con1) and a call with an argument awaiting its call (nt1) take IsSource's verdict as f1 does (C-359
    // B1, F's O1 (a)); `t is owner` alone forms (fr4cv, con1o). The invalid
    // rows' record is the owner's O-332 (a). A reference at a required Type whose closed leaf layer `s/Box` meets `Box` is not on the
    // split: the leaf is an exact source (the owner's O-338 (a)), and its owner evidence and U's undetermined outer Semantics do not
    // agree (IsSource, D3 revision 2: p3's Language verdict, SPEC 10.8), so fr1w (which 2f4bec489 accepted) has p3's record at the
    // reference and rf1 (a reference in a candidate's argument, which 2f4bec489 accepted) at the call; rf1o is its `t is owner` twin.
    [Theory]
