    // split is still erased in its environment, whose Owned proof reads only the bound Type arguments: a Language failure of its own at
    // its own node, as on dev. A written argument takes it (fx4 = fr4x, `put3<U>`; fr3x, the container's `S<U>`), and the reference, a
    // verdict over that failed child, adds no record; with none written the reference takes it (fr2). Its twins: only the split (fx1,
    // `U is Owned`) and only Owned (fx2, `t is owner`). 09251209c gave fx4, fr3x and fr2 the split's Unsupported_Kd alone. The same
    // wherever the erasure is judged (C-359 C2): a reference to a group (b4g, b4go its split-only twin), a Function Item an argument of
    // the one resting candidate erases, its record the part's as on dev (b4a, b4ao; b4c with the callee's argument written), and an Item
    // value at an initialization (ev1); 1cabcd14d gave b4g, b4a and b4c the split's Unsupported_Kd alone and ev1 TypeMismatch_Kd. The
    // erasure fails once, at its first argument not proven Owned (b4m, `put5<U, U>`: 1cabcd14d recorded both). Several candidates
    // that rest on the split and all declare the part at a Function Type erase it whichever a case selects (c2g, two `take`; c2go its
    // split-only twin): fe40945ac judged the Owned part only where one candidate rested and gave c2g Unsupported_Kd alone. Beside an
    // applicable candidate that takes the part as it is (`take<Z, F>(z: Z, f: F)`), no case erases it (SPEC 10.2.2: the owner case is
    // ambiguous, every other selects the second), so no Owned requirement arises and the call rests on the split (c2h; c2ho with
    // `U is Owned`): 32f0cde25 read only the pending candidates and gave c2h an Owned UnprovenConstraint_Kd.
