    // SPEC 8.1.1, 8.15.2, 10.1.1, 10.2, 10.7, 23.1.2 (C-359 C1; DECISIONS D3 with rule W, Q13 rule 3): a check on the unformed split
    // whose binder is fixed before any evidence (a Function Item's bound arguments, a reference's written ones) is judged in each case
    // of the split layer: one that fails in every case fails by itself and keeps its Language record, as on dev, and only one that some
    // case takes rests on the split (Unsupported_Kd, the owner's O-332 (a)). A value call through `put3<U>`: a Tag or `true` at `s/Box`
    // (vc1, vc2), a missing or extra argument (vc3, vc4), a Tag at `m` (vc5); the direct call with the argument written (dc1, dc2). A
    // reference at S: a Tag where S needs `s/Box` (rfMo; rfM without `U is Owned`; rfMm a member; rfMg a group), a result or a later
    // written argument S contradicts (rfR, rfM2); `ref/Box` meets the ref case, so rfB rests on the split. An Item erased at an
    // argument, in either order (b4a2, b4a3), and at an initialization (ev2; ev1o meets the owner case and rests on the split).
    // 1cabcd14d gave every row but rfB and ev2 Unsupported_Kd (rfM the Owned record alone; ev1o TypeMismatch_Kd). With two bindings
    // that form no Type (`put7<U, V>`), the cases are their combinations, whichever binding the misfit is at: a Tag at `s/Box` (r2p;
    // d2p its direct call) or at `q/Box` (r2q; v2c the value call of a premise-free put7, beside put7's own case-limit record), while
    // `(U, V, Box, ref/Box)` meets the combination owner, ref and rests on the split (r2v). fe40945ac formed only the first binding
    // a case met and gave r2q and v2c Unsupported_Kd.
