    public void ACheckThatFailsInEveryCaseOfTheSplitKeepsItsLanguageRecord(string source, string records)
        => Assert.Equal(records, DiagnosticCorpus.RecordProfile(source));

    // SPEC 8.15.2, 3.5.2, 23.1.2 (C-359 E1, E2, E3; G812 rulings 102-104; DECISIONS D3): a check on the split is a list of parts, and a
    // failure belongs to the part that fails. A member call's typed part at a layer of the receiver's container binder is judged in
    // each case as a frame slot's is (dM1: a Tag at `s/Box` over `S<U>`; dM2 the split only; dM5 no split). A part that forms no
    // Type in any case (a direct target, `n: W`) is unknown and the next part is judged, whatever the parameter order (dtA, dtA2;
    // dtB the order that already held; dtD1, dtE1, dtV1 controls). A binding's cases are those its premises admit: under `U is Copy`
    // no uniq or object layer (sC1, sC2, sC3; `ref/Box` is admitted and rests, sC0). A failing run blames only the bindings its
    // failing part read, so a misfit behind eight bindings is decided in nine runs (r8r, r8i, v4r; r4q the control), also where one
    // parameter's structural walk meets every layer (rH, rH0, r8h; r8hv, no misfit, rests) and where two parts over one binding fail
    // only together (eAB). An Item's signature fit is parts too (eN2, grouped at the call). 155a76cbe gave dM1, dtA, dtA2, sC1-sC3,
    // r8r, r8i, v4r, r8h and eN2 Unsupported_Kd. The contract's walk names the member that misfits inside a parameter's nested Callable
    // signature, and that member is the failing part (G812 ruling 105): an Item whose parameter `h: (s0/Box, s1/Box) -> i32` holds
    // layers of two bindings is judged in the nine cases of the one that misfits (eIH at `s1`, eIH2 at `s0`; eIHv, no misfit, rests).
    // 95629c6b4 blamed both bindings and gave eIH and eIH2 Unsupported_Kd at the bound.
    // A layer below a compared layer is compared with the part that layer's case formed, so its misfit is blamed on both bindings
    // (G812 ruling 106, C-I1): `n: s0/(s1/Box)` meets `ref/(objref/Box)` in the one combination ref, objref and rests (nL), and
    // `ref/(objref/Tag)` in none (nLo). 7c03c23d1 blamed the inner binding alone and gave nL TypeMismatch_Kd. putN's nested layer
    // has its own MissingOriginBinding_Kd in both rows: no spelling without it was found.
    // A value call's argument that fails at an element of a Tuple parameter fails by that element, which its fit names (the owner's
    // O-392 (c), G812 ruling 109): a Tag at the third element of `n: (s0/Box during a, s1/Box during b, s2/Box during c)` is judged
    // in the nine cases of `s2`, for a Tuple literal (eT3c) and a typed value (eT3t), also below a nested Tuple (eT3n, eT3tn);
    // elements that fit every case, or only the owner cases, rest (eT3cv, eT3tv). 551cc37c6 blamed the three bindings and gave
    // eT3c, eT3t, eT3n and eT3tn Unsupported_Kd at the bound.
    // The fit names every component that formation keeps in its position, not a Tuple's element only (G812 ruling 111): the Tag
    // below `Option<(...)>` (eT3o), as an argument of `Two<s0/Box during a, s1/Box during b>` (eT3w), in an array literal's Tuple
    // (eT3a) and below a written layer `ref/(...)`, for a typed value and a borrowed literal (eT3L, eT3Lc), is judged in nine
    // cases; their twins that fit in the owner cases rest (eT3ov, eT3wv, eT3Lv). be6a64efe gave eT3o, eT3w, eT3a, eT3L and
    // eT3Lc Unsupported_Kd at the bound.
    // A join's result formed part by part fails by the component of its child position too (G812 ruling 114, C-R1): `p: (Box,
    // ref/Box)` in a join's Tuple at `n: ((s0/Box during a, s1/Box during b), s2/Box during c)` meets `s1/Box` only where s1 is ref
    // and rests (jJ), as `(b0@move, b1@ref)` nested in it does (jJnv). 529b15159 named the child's component against the child's own
    // Type, blamed `s2` (jJ) or `s0` (jJnv) and gave both NoApplicableOverload_Kd.
